From ec62d2c7b5c39cfd8e7ee7939ca9e57a0b36e237 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:26:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/92] moe-stream : the router's mailbox (SiegeLadder G16,
 g3-design.md step 1), on by default - at decode the remap's card inputs (the
 ids, the drop rule's packed input, runahead's prediction) go through pinned
 host records the card posts into with a new op, GGML_OP_MBOX_POST (CUDA: one
 block copies the payload, a system-scope fence, then the record's sequence
 word +1; a CPU version too), and the remap ops read them instead of the
 scheduler's copy: their CPU split has no card input, so no synchronize and no
 copy before it, and the shared expert (now built ahead on every path) runs on
 the card while the host remaps. The host polls the sequence word, flushes the
 compute stream at once and every ms (ggml_backend_cuda_stream_query, WDDM),
 and aborts after 30 s; the records need unified addressing (checked with
 ggml_backend_cuda_host_device_ptr). SiegeLadder runs.md 4.74: text = trace,
 the deterministic counters equal to the unit; runahead off 12.15 -> 12.90
 tok/s, exact runahead +3.3%, the drop default +6.2%.
 LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_MAILBOX=0 - the scheduler's copy

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
